    "body": "### Problem\n\nCurrently there is no reliable way to display virtual line with its own highlighting *till the end of line*. This type of feature is important when virtual lines are used to display diff-style information, like a reference text {i.e. before the change} of the line.\n\nThere is hack to append a wide enough whitespace suffix with a dedicated `EOL` highlight group ...\n\n```lua\nlocal virt_lines = { { { 'Virtual line', 'String' }, { string.rep(' ', vim.o.columns), 'Visual' } } }\nvim.api.nvim_buf_set_extmark(0, ns_id, 0, 0, { virt_lines = virt_lines })\n```\n\n... but it works only if the virtual line doesn't wrap along with the text (which is now possible thanks to #40113). If virtual line wraps with text (i.e. `virt_lines_overflow` is set to `'wrap'` or `'auto'`), then the suffix will also be displayed in the wrapped part of the virtual line. Dynamically computing the suffix width is not possible since the same buffer can be displayed in several windows with different width while extmarks are set per buffer. I.e. like this:\n\n<img width=\"800\" height=\"600\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0e257912-7698-4358-830e-001e2fbe5274\" />\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nA way to tell extmark that its virtual lines need to highlight till the end of line.\n\nFor example, a new `virt_lines_eol_hl_grup` option that would contain a highlight group used to add end-of-line style highlighting for every virtual line. With this approach, the above example would be replicated as `vim.api.nvim_buf_set_extmark(0, ns_id, 0, 0, { virt_lines = { { { 'Virtual line', 'String' } } }, virt_lines_eol_hl_group = 'Visual' })`\n\nAnother approach might be to allow a special chunk at the end of the virtual line list to mean \"use this highlight group till the the of line\". Like, for example, `{ true, 'Visual' }`. The above example is then implemented with `vim.api.nvim_buf_set_extmark(0, ns_id, 0, 0, { virt_lines = { { { 'Virtual line', 'String' }, { true, 'Visual' } } } })`. This approach is more flexible as it allows more granular control over which lines highlight till end of line and with what highlight group, but it also widens the data structure of a text-hl chunk. It might be reasonable to use empty string instead of `true`, but not sure if this is intuitive enough.",
